```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: WMI Process Execution from Remote Source (Lateral Tooling)
# Detection ID: DE-EX-002
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1047 - Windows Management Instrumentation
# Data Source: Sysmon EventCode=1, WmiPrvSE parent
# Severity: Medium
# ============================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
ParentImage="*\\WmiPrvSE.exe"
| stats count min(_time) as first_seen values(CommandLine) as cmd values(Image) as child by ComputerName, User
| eval first_seen=strftime(first_seen,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| where count>0
| sort -count
```

## Detection Logic
WmiPrvSE.exe spawning a child process almost always indicates remote WMI execution (wmic process call create, Invoke-WmiMethod, or Impacket wmiexec.py) rather than local user activity.

## False Positive Considerations
SCCM, monitoring agents, and some backup tools use WMI legitimately — allowlist their service accounts.

## Tuning Notes
Cross-reference User field against a service-account allowlist lookup to cut noise before triage.
